Review the diff below for HACKY PATTERNS:

1. Redundant state, cached values that could be derived
2. Parameter sprawl on new functions
3. Copy-paste with slight variation
4. Leaky abstractions (exposing internals that should be encapsulated)
5. Stringly-typed code where constants/enums exist
6. Nested conditionals 3+ levels deep
7. Unnecessary comments explaining WHAT (vs WHY)

Focus on:
- The new `enable_kanata_roi()` method in `verilator/src/simulator.hpp` and its validation block in `verilator/src/main.cpp`. Are the four error paths (kanata_file empty / loop_gate set / clarity_file / hybrid_icount / resume_from_qemu) redundant with what enable_kanata_roi itself checks? Look for double validation between main.cpp and simulator.hpp.
- The `RoiKanataGate` struct vs `kanata::LoopGate` -- two near-identical structs?
- The Python kanata/objdump validation in `hsim` (~lines 250-280): could it fold into the existing pc-mode validation block?
- Comments in `verilator/src/hybrid/kanata_roi.hpp` and `verilator/src/simulator.hpp::enable_kanata_roi` -- do they narrate WHAT or capture non-obvious WHY?
- The bash awk script in tests/hsim/test_hsim_kanata.sh (steps 4 and 5) -- duplicated objdump invocations? Magic numbers (`7c005073`, `7c00d073`)?
- `tests/e2e.sh` array building -- is `VSIM_KANATA_ARGS` truly parallel to `VSIM_TRIG_ARGS`, or does it have spurious differences?

REPORT ONLY: each finding as `file:line - issue - suggested fix`. Skip nits that don't change correctness or clarity. Under 400 words.

=== FULL DIFF ===

# verilator/src/hybrid/csr_trigger.hpp
Added pcs_of_kind(kind) returning sorted vector<uint64_t> of PCs matching kind. Walks hits_ (unordered_map<uint64_t, CsrTriggerHit>), filters, sorts.

# verilator/src/hybrid/handoff_controller.hpp
Added `auto trigger() const -> const Trigger& { return trigger_; }`.

# verilator/src/hybrid/kanata_roi.hpp (NEW)
```cpp
namespace hybrid {

struct RoiKanataGate {
  uint64_t start_pc;
  uint64_t end_pc;
  uint64_t skip_iters;
  uint64_t record_iters;
};

inline auto derive_roi_kanata_gate(
  const CsrTrigger& trigger, uint64_t resume_pc,
  std::optional<uint64_t> explicit_exit_pc) -> RoiKanataGate
{
  uint64_t end_pc = 0;
  if (explicit_exit_pc) {
    end_pc = *explicit_exit_pc;
  } else {
    const auto exits = trigger.pcs_of_kind(HYBRID_HANDOFF_EXIT);
    if (exits.empty()) {
      throw std::runtime_error("--kanata-roi: no csrwi 0x7C0,1 (EXIT) marker found in ELF -- use --mode pc with --pc-end");
    }
    if (exits.size() > 1) {
      throw std::runtime_error("--kanata-roi: " + std::to_string(exits.size()) + " csrwi 0x7C0,1 (EXIT) markers in ELF -- use --mode pc with an explicit --pc-end to disambiguate");
    }
    end_pc = exits.front();
  }
  return RoiKanataGate{resume_pc, end_pc, 0u, 1u};
}
}
```

For reference, kanata::LoopGate (existing, in src/pipeview/kanata_logger.hpp) has identical layout: {start_pc, end_pc, skip_iters, record_iters} all uint64_t.

# verilator/src/simulator.hpp
```cpp
void enable_kanata_roi(const std::string& filename,
                       const std::string& objdump_file,
                       std::optional<uint64_t> explicit_exit_pc)
{
  if (!hybrid_input_state_)
    throw std::runtime_error("--kanata-roi requires --resume-from-qemu (no resume PC available)");
  if (!hybrid_handoff_)
    throw std::runtime_error("--kanata-roi requires CSR or PC trigger mode (incompatible with --hybrid-icount)");
  const auto gate = hybrid::derive_roi_kanata_gate(
    hybrid_handoff_->trigger(), hybrid_input_state_->pc, explicit_exit_pc);
  spdlog::info("kanata-roi: window start=0x{:x} end=0x{:x} (skip=0 record=1)",
               gate.start_pc, gate.end_pc);
  trace_.enable_kanata(cpu, filename, objdump_file,
    kanata::LoopGate{gate.start_pc, gate.end_pc, gate.skip_iters, gate.record_iters});
}
```

# verilator/src/main.cpp -- validation block
```cpp
if (args.kanata_roi) {
  if (args.kanata_file.empty())
    throw std::runtime_error("--kanata-roi requires --kanata <file>");
  if (loop_gate)
    throw std::runtime_error("--kanata-roi and --kanata-loop-* are mutually exclusive");
  if (!args.clarity_file.empty())
    throw std::runtime_error("--kanata-roi is not supported with --clarity");
  if (args.hybrid_icount)
    throw std::runtime_error("--kanata-roi is incompatible with --hybrid-icount (no single exit PC); use --mode csr or --mode pc instead");
  if (args.resume_from_qemu.empty())
    throw std::runtime_error("--kanata-roi requires --resume-from-qemu");
}
if (!args.kanata_file.empty() && !args.kanata_roi)
  sim.enable_kanata(args.kanata_file, args.objdump_file, loop_gate);
```

Then later (after enable_hybrid_handoff):
```cpp
if (args.kanata_roi)
  sim.enable_kanata_roi(args.kanata_file, args.objdump_file, args.hybrid_exit_pc);
```

